// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - WebFabData 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1313733115" "Web construction files"
// DetailString :
"P3430908489" "The blueprints and data Arbiter Sands was carrying when you captured him might provide a clue to the Web's true purpose."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - PartialCoordinates1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P954841850" "Portal Data - Korol"
// DetailString :
"P2999292502" "You got this part of the data you'll need to get back to your own time from Regent Korol, the leader of the cybernetic Tarantula Queens of Arachnos. It contains the current date, and part of the code you'll need to open the doors to the portal chamber. According to the data, this twisted future is less than 1 year away, should Recluse activate the Web."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - PartialCoordinates2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P68826688" "Portal Data 2 - Mu'Drakhan"
// DetailString :
"P760581412" "You recovered this part of the portal data you'll need to return to your own time from Magus Mu'Drakhan, leader of Arachnos's Mu Mystics. This data includes part of the door codes, as well as precise data on the levels of magical energy in the world, vital for calibrating a time-gate. It's shocking information, detailing a world where magic is dying, along with vast numbers of peoples and cultures."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - PartialCoordinates3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2190409619" "Portal Data 3 - Shadow Spider"
// DetailString :
"P2087259618" "You recovered this part of the time portal's setting data and entry codes from Shadow Spider, Spymaster of Arachnos. Along with her part of the entry codes, her information also contained details of the labyrinthine security protecting the portal. Pages of security measures, traps, and counter-measures reveal the paranoid nature of Recluse's totalitarian ideal."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - PartialCoordinates4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3843875429" "Portal Data 4 - Viridian"
// DetailString :
"P3085287230" "You recovered this data from Viridian, Arachnos's counter-intelligence expert. Along with his portion of the door codes are the precise dimensional coordinates needed to properly calibrate the time portal. They also list dozens of other dimensions that are being invaded or are about to be attacked by Arachnos. Recluse's ambitions do not stop at one world, he intends to cover the multiverse in the shadow of his megalomania. <br><br>Curiously, the palmtop computer that held this information is also filled with episodes of various soap operas."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - LabCodeFragment1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1889761766" "The 1st Lab Code - Wretch"
// DetailString :
"P143178578" "You got this part of the code to enter Dr. Aeon's Lab from the Wretch, Ghost Widow's mutated bodyguard. There is a short note stuck to it. It reads: <br><br>'Protect Dr. Aeon, my Wretch, but watch him, too. He promises Lord Recluse great power, but I fear he is loyal only to himself and his own scientific madness.' <br>The note is not signed, but sealed with a black kiss."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - LabCodeFragment2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P743088848" "The 2nd Lab Code - Silver Mantis"
// DetailString :
"P3986466327" "You got this part of the code to enter Dr. Aeon's Lab from Silver Mantis, Arachnos's top assassin and the rumored lover of Black Scorpion. Along with her part of the code, you also found a great deal of technical data stolen from the Aeoncorp mainframe. Looks like she had been doing a bit of extra industrial espionage work for Black Scorpion on the side."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - LabCodeFragment3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P952329796" "The 3rd Lab Code - Barracuda"
// DetailString :
"P1454999618" "You got this part of the code to enter Dr. Aeon's Lab from Barracuda, Captain Mako's protege. You can barely make out the codes on the paper, because it's covered with strange drawings of what look like enormous shark teeth and a gigantic eye."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - LabCodeFragment4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1807760106" "The 4th Lab Code - Ice Mistral"
// DetailString :
"P1343083936" "You got this part of the code to enter Dr. Aeon's Lab from Ice Mistral, the young villainess Scirocco has been training. The code was tucked into a thick fashion magazine she had been reading. A quick flip through the magazine shows that she'd tried all the perfume samples, and had been scratching out the faces of all the female models."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - AllCodesGathered 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3985488960" "The Full lab code"
// DetailString :
"P2212773526" "Now that you've gathered all the fragments from your fallen foes, you can finally enter Dr. Aeon's lab and bring him to justice."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SecretOfTheWeb 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3847933178" "The Secret of the Web"
// DetailString :
"P226680124" "'What does the web do?' Dr. Aeon sneers as you push him through the portal. 'It is my ultimate triumph. I doubt you could comprehend it, but I'll use small words to help you. It uses science and magic together, Techno-magic, if you will, to drain super human powers. You heard me right! It drains super-powers, but instead of simply making them go away like the clumsy spells of the Mu, it transfers them. YES! They said it couldn't be done, but they also said it was foolish to tap a bound demon to power a city, but I did it! I did it! The Web then transfers those stolen energies into a specific individual. Oh, you'll have quite a time stopping Recluse's plans, once he controls the power of every meta-human on Earth! And all because of my meta-human scientific genius! Ah-HAH-HAH-HAH-HAH-WAAAit a second! <br>If he get every meta-human ability... <br>Then he'd get my... <br>I'd be just... <br>Uh-oh! You've got to stop him!'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - BuildingKey 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1833491486" "Aeon Corporation entry key"
// DetailString :
"P29550751" "Though it took some hunting, you found the real security key for the Aeon Corp building on the real Security Chief. Now to get into that building and catch Dr. Aeon!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3879063021" "Ms. Liberty's Task Force - Part 1"
// DetailString :
"P3043586738" "It all started when you learned that Ms. Liberty needed your help. It seems that Lord Recluse was close to completing the mysterious device known as 'The Web' on Grandville Island, and while no one knew it's true purpose, rumors were flying that Lord Recluse believed it would somehow make him the master of the world. You traveled to the Web Fabrication factory just outside of Grandville, where you gathered vital data and did enough damage to slow down the Web's completion."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3424165422" "Ms. Liberty's Task Force - Part 2"
// DetailString :
"P1029164126" "It all started when you learned that Ms. Liberty needed your help. It seems that Lord Recluse was close to completing the mysterious device known as 'The Web' on Grandville Island, and while no one knew it's true purpose, rumors were flying that Lord Recluse believed it would somehow make him the master of the world. You traveled to the Web Fabrication factory just outside of Grandville, where you gathered vital data and did enough damage to slow down the Web's completion. <br><br> The files you found revealed that the Web had been designed by Dr. Aeon, a Mad Scientist in Recluse's employ. You tried to use a portal to capture him in his base, but the wily scientist tricked you, hurtling you to a future where Recluse was triumphant and the world was under Arachnos control! You barely escaped by over-riding another portal, but the chilling message was there: If Recluse wins out, it could be the end of freedom in the world."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission3Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3573788527" "Ms. Liberty's Task Force - Part 3"
// DetailString :
"P2112941863" "It all started when you learned that Ms. Liberty needed your help. It seems that Lord Recluse was close to completing the mysterious device known as 'The Web' on Grandville Island, and while no one knew it's true purpose, rumors were flying that Lord Recluse believed it would somehow make him the master of the world. You traveled to the Web Fabrication factory just outside of Grandville, where you gathered vital data and did enough damage to slow down the Web's completion. <br><br> The files you found revealed that the Web had been designed by Dr. Aeon, a Mad Scientist in Recluse's employ. You tried to use a portal to capture him in his base, but the wily scientist tricked you, hurtling you to a future where Recluse was triumphant and the world was under Arachnos control! You barely escaped by over-riding another portal, but the chilling message was there: If Recluse wins out, it could be the end of freedom in the world. <br><br>On Numina's advice, you sought a way to keep Dr. Aeon from using any more tricks to elude capture. To do that, you had to travel to Thorn Island, where the Circle of Thorns were feeding mystic energy to a great Tree of Thorns for their own dire purposes. You disrupted their plans and captured the energy of the tree for your own, to use against Dr. Aeon when the time came."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission4Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2588031400" "Ms. Liberty's Task Force - Part 4"
// DetailString :
"P822435164" "It all started when you learned that Ms. Liberty needed your help. It seems that Lord Recluse was close to completing the mysterious device known as 'The Web' on Grandville Island, and while no one knew it's true purpose, rumors were flying that Lord Recluse believed it would somehow make him the master of the world. You traveled to the Web Fabrication factory just outside of Grandville, where you gathered vital data and did enough damage to slow down the Web's completion. <br><br> The files you found revealed that the Web had been designed by Dr. Aeon, a Mad Scientist in Recluse's employ. You tried to use a portal to capture him in his base, but the wily scientist tricked you, hurtling you to a future where Recluse was triumphant and the world was under Arachnos control! You barely escaped by over-riding another portal, but the chilling message was there: If Recluse wins out, it could be the end of freedom in the world. <br><br>On Numina's advice, you sought a way to keep Dr. Aeon from using any more tricks to elude capture. To do that, you had to travel to Thorn Island, where the Circle of Thorns were feeding mystic energy to a great Tree of Thorns for their own dire purposes. You disrupted their plans and captured the energy of the tree for your own, to use against Dr. Aeon when the time came. <br><br>With the power of the Thorn tree, you went to Cap Au Diable to bring the mad doctor to justice. After fighting your way through the lieutenants of each member of Lord Recluse's inner circle, you confronted Dr. Aeon and his time duplicates. While you were able to catch Aeon this time, he revealed the true purpose of the Web: It was designed to siphon the powers of every other metahuman on Earth into Lord Recluse, rendering him invincible!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL9_Taskforce_Statesman_Souvenir_Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P2076265531" "The Helm of Recluse"
// tDetailString :
"P2018373025" "Though battered from the mighty battle where you faced it's owner, none can deny that this is the helmet of Lord Recluse himself, master of Arachnos and the Regent of the Rogue Isles. But even he couldn't stop you and your team when you faced him at the pulse-pounding culmination of Ms. Liberty's Task Force. <br><br>It all started when you learned that Ms. Liberty needed your help. It seems that Lord Recluse was close to completing the mysterious device known as 'The Web' on Grandville Island, and while no one knew it's true purpose, rumors were flying that Lord Recluse believed it would somehow make him the master of the world. You traveled to the Web Fab factory just outside of Grandville, where you gathered vital data and did enough damage to slow down the Web's completion. <br><br> The files you found revealed that the Web had been designed by Dr. Aeon, a Mad Scientist in Recluse's employ. You tried to use a portal to capture him in his base, but the wily scientist tricked you, hurtling you to a future where Recluse was triumphant and the world was under Arachnos control! You barely escaped by over-riding another portal, but the chilling message was there: If Recluse wins out, it could be the end of freedom in the world. <br><br>On Numina's advice, you sought a way to keep Dr. Aeon from using any more tricks to elude capture. To do that, you had to travel to Thorn Island, where the Circle of Thorns were feeding mystic energy to a great Tree of Thorns for their own dire purposes. You disrupted their plans and captured the energy of the tree for your own, to use against Dr. Aeon when the time came. <br><br>With the power of the Thorn tree, you went to Cap Au Diable to bring the mad doctor to justice. After fighting your way through the lieutenants of each member of Lord Recluse's inner circle, you confronted Dr. Aeon and his time duplicates. While you were able to catch Aeon this time, he revealed the true purpose of the Web: It was designed to siphon the powers of every other metahuman on Earth into Lord Recluse, rendering him invincible! <br><br>With the Freedom Phalanx paralyzed as the first targets of the Web, Ms. Liberty had to send you to take on Lord Recluse yourselves. And that you did. Legends will be told about the battle that day, as the very  foundations of Grandville trembled beneath the mighty forces unleashed in the final battle. But when you hold this helmet, you know what those legends will say. That in the darkest hour this world has ever known, Heroes stood strong and cast that darkness back. And they will always stand ready to do so."

