// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P856364347" ""
// AcceptString :
"P200102558" "Begin Ms. Liberty's Task Force"
// SendOffString :
"P165044482" "<color deepskyblue>Ms. Liberty TASKFORCE:  'The Weaving of the Web' <br>Part: One<br><br></color>I'm glad to have you all aboard. Your first mission will be to <color lightgreen>delay the Web's completion by disrupting production in the Web Fabrication facility</color>, a factory-island near Grandville. We'll be sending you in by submarine. <br><br>You'll have 2 objectives: <br>First, you'll need to destroy structural parts of the Web under production to help slow down construction and buy us the time we need to learn what's Recluse is planning. <br><br>Secondly, your actions should be enough to draw out the Web Fabrication's overseer, a cunning and ruthless young Arbiter named <color red>Sands</color>. Capturing him will throw their operation into chaos and set them back even farther. Sands is a smart character, so we may even be able to learn some information from him. Once you're done, get back to the submarine and return to Paragon City."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3980773873" "Disrupt Web Factory"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P839667105" "<color deepskyblue>Ms. Liberty TASKFORCE:  'The Weaving of the Web' <br>Part: One<br><br></color>Arachnos will try to stop us, but we must persevere. The first step is to destroy as many pieces of the Web as you can then capture Arbiter Sands."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P4108721617" "The Rogue Isles. You can see Grandville from here, the lair of Lord Recluse himself. Your mission today is in the Web Fabrication facility, but the shrouded sight of Recluse's city of villains hovers in the back of your mind like a shadow."
// Script Variable DisplayText :
"P2980529692" "Web Parts to Destroy"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2297724426" "Security Squad Leader"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1259970715" "<shout>Kill the intruders!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P391729625" "<shout>Eliminate all non-Arachnos personnel!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// CutScene 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// 4 B_Boss :
"P2924948505" "<em drink>I go to Grandville for some decent coffee and this is what happens?"
// 6 B_Boss :
"P3384933228" "<em Plot>Well, adopt, adapt, and improve, I suppose. At least it will give me a chance to re-organize things after we clean up. "
// 5 B_Boss :
"P2523631885" "<em crack>Though no doubt I'll have to annihilate the persons responsible first. How bothersome."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3187534667" "Arbiter Sands"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3256338359" "<shout>Well, I think I've had just about enough of this."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P4046460251" "For Arachnos, etcetera, For Lord Recluse, etcetera etcetera."
// Script Variable BOSS_1STBLOOD_DIALOG :
"P2397969411" "I'm a busy man, so if you'd just die right now, that will be fine."
// Script Variable BOSS_75HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P3981451886" "You seem to have harmed me. How importunate."
// Script Variable BOSS_50HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P1108413438" "I don't recall if I've told you that you vex me."
// Script Variable BOSS_25HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P3689165749" "Do you people have any idea what this is doing to my schedule?"
// Script Variable BOSS_DEAD_DIALOG :
"P1887238262" " Indeed, you are terribly vexsome. <em>And I don't say that to many people."
// Script Variable BOSS_KILLEDHERO_DIALOG :
"P2251611777" "Well, that's one cookie crumbled."
// Script Variable BOSS_KILLEDHERO_DIALOG :
"P1502418191" "I don't mind telling you I took some degree of satisfaction in that."
// Script Variable BOSS_KILLEDHERO_DIALOG :
"P2799756562" "Hail Lord Recluse, etcetera, etcetera. <em>We destroy your enemies, etcetera, etcetera."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - SandsBlasted 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P3503868766" "Capture Arbiter Sands"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1008029383" "You have captured Arbiter Sands"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2238293358" "It's time to get out of the Web Fabrication facility!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1141508347" "<color deepskyblue>Ms. Liberty:  'The Weaving of the Web' <br>Part: One<br><br></color>Good to see you made it out. Arachnos has gone into high alert while they try to figure out what we know, and that combined with your work will slow down their production and give us the time we need. <br><br>The information you found has told us something important. Our initial pass shows the Web bears all of the design hallmarks of one of Arachnos's most depraved mad geniuses: <color red>Dr. Aeon</color>. Capturing him might provide all the remaining answers we need in time to stop Lord Recluse."
// RandomFameString :
"P4011708702" "I think something big is going on, and I keep hearing people talk about {TaskForceName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P15760484" "<color deepskyblue>Ms. Liberty TASKFORCE:  'Evil's Foresight' <br>Part: Two<br><br></color>The files you found in the factory prove that the Web was designed by one of Lord Recluse's pet mad scientists, <color red>Dr. Aeon</color>. SERAPH scientists are trying to reverse engineer his work, but by then it might be too late. If we're going to get the answers we're looking for in time to stop Recluse, we'll need to <color lightgreen>bring in Dr. Aeon himself.</color>"
// AcceptString :
"P2739687221" "Capture Dr. Aeon"
// SendOffString :
"P2234505356" "<color deepskyblue>Ms. Liberty TASKFORCE:  'Evil's Foresight' <br>Part: Two<br><br></color>We've developed a plan to catch Dr. Aeon by surprise in one of his own labs. We've set up a portal that will send you directly into Dr. Aeon's portal lab in Cap Au Diable. <br><br><color lightgreen>Once there, you're to locate and capture Dr. Aeon</color>, then over-ride one of his portals and return to Portal Corp. I suggest you stock up on inspirations before you leave, since <Color Red>you won't be able to return to Paragon City until this is over.</Color>"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4244508694" "<color deepskyblue>Ms. Liberty  TASKFORCE:  'Evil's Foresight' <br>Part: Two<br><br></color>Don't let any of Aeon's tricks throw you off. Persevere, heroes."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P8244934" "You enter the portal and find yourselves in Dr. Aeon's lab, somewhere in Cap Au Diable. The mad doctor is here somewhere. The only question is what nasty surprise does he has in store for you?"

